      "side": 1,
      "message": "Right now, as if the command doesn\u0027t exist, since in this case the symlink shouldn\u0027t have even been set up. But if it was for some reason:\n\nThe tool itself will print this message in the stderr, and exit with a failure -- which may or may not be visible in the kati/ninja output depending on what ran it.\n\nWe\u0027ll also have sent off a logging message above, and the current implementation in soong_ui will abort with an error message, including the full argument list, but not any other process information currently. Since it\u0027s fatal, we probably don\u0027t even get the failure from ninja.\n\nI had an implementation here that called out to pstree, but that\u0027s not available on Mac. I\u0027ll probably write an implementation that parses \u0027ps -o pid,ppid,command\u0027, since that seems to be the most stable common interface.",
